{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513609-giants","id":1513609,"title":"Giants","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-01T23:41:46-07:00","id":1513609,"title":"Giants","content":"Good evening class!<br /> <br /> Tonight's topic will be an interesting question<br /> Have you ever used Giants in your chronicle?<br /> <br /> The Players Guide to the Sabbat 1992 edition gave us a nice vampiric artifact called:<br /> <b>Giant's Blood</b><br /> This is exactly what it reads - giants\u2019 blood. In the ancient days when the giants walked the earth, only foolhardy vampires would prey upon these loathsome creatures. A few vampires did, however, and they made sure they bottled the remainder of the prized blood that they could not consume immediately. The blood, at least temporarily, and possibly permanently, increases vampire\u2019s Potence score dramatically.<br /> <br /> In Dark Alliance: Vancouver, there is the Slumbering Giant, a 4th Generation Gangrel, sire of Mictantecle<br /> The Slumbering Giant is an epithet for an ancient Gangrel methuselah that lies in torpor under the Simon Fraser University at Vancouver<br /> Dark Ages supplements suggest, there are Giants in Scandinavia and far North and they are the spwans of Caine - prompting many Cainite expeditions to discover them and their secrets, but none of those expeditions returned<br /> <br /> To toss a real life legend in to the mix, the Solomon Islands have become an interesting place of myth and folklore in recent years<br /> the indigenous people, as well as the folklore surrounding them.<br /> The Solomon Island Giants were said to be over 10 feet tall, with evidence that suggests the giants can grow much taller and supposedly inhabit caves throughout the islands.<br /> The surprising features of the Solomon Island Giants are similar to other creatures around the world, like Bigfoot and the Mongolian Almas. They have very long black, brown or reddish hair, bulging double eyebrows, red eyes, flat noses, and large mouths.<br /> There are thought to be 3 different species of giant, the largest over 10 feet tall, with another being smaller, and the third smaller still \u2013 but still bigger than a human.<br /> The Books Solomon Islands Mysteries said: \u201cIt is linguistically ironic that the Solomon Islands\u2019 people name their \u201cundiscovered to the modern world\u201d race of hominoids \u201cthe giants\u201d, as throughout history, including in the Bible and other prominent books, the same name has been used in other parts of the world to describe these huge, elusive subterranean hominoids.\u201d<br /> Marius Boirayon, the author, writes that some of the giants were killing and stealing humans from their villages. He speaks of a huge rogue \u201ckiller giant\u201d attacking the indigenous people.<br /> \u201cThis monstrous giant was an elusive and cunning creature that stalked its victims and often crept around the villages at night to seek its meals\u201d Marius writes.<br /> He goes on to explain that many warriors had died trying to slay the giant, before villages had to be moved to other parts of the islands in order to protect their people.<br /> The Solomon Island Giants are said to have social structures, and there are possibly thousands of them which inhabit Guadalcanal to this day. They use complex cave systems to pass from one side of the island to the other, without ever having to see daylight.<br /> \u200bBetween 1942-45, Japanese and U.S forces engaged in heavy fighting on the islands, which became known as the Solomon Islands campaign.<br /> During this conflict, Japanese forces would experience first hand encounters with the Solomon Island Giants.<br /> They reported seeing creatures around 10 to 15 feet tall, which would sometimes come charging at units of soldiers. Their bullets had little effect on them.<br /> While suffering from attacks in daylight, soldiers also had hard time sleeping, as they could hear their fellow comrades wailing through the night as the giants launched more attacks. The cannibalistic nature of the giants struck fear in the hearts of the Japanese infantry.<br /> The giants of the Solomon Islands are common knowledge to locals, but along with stories of foreign encounters and sightings of footprints, there could be more truth to the stories than we realize...<br /> <br /> Other Legends tie the Solomon Island Giants to the Nephilim, saying they are either surviving Nephilims either/or their descendants<br /> The Book of Enoch says: they were &quot;great giants, whose height was three hundred cubits&quot;. (A cubit being 18 inches (46 cm), this would make them 450 feet (140 m) tall.)<br /> The Quran refers to the people of \u0100d in Quran 26:130 whom the prophet Hud declares to be like jabbarin (Hebrew: gibborim), probably a reference to the Biblical Nephilim. The people of \u0100d are said to be giants, the tallest among them 100 ft (30 m) high<br /> \u200bReferences to the offspring of Seth rebelling from God and mingling with the daughters of Cain are found from the second century CE onwards in both Christian and Jewish sources - the view expressed in the modern canonical Amharic Ethiopian Orthodox Bible: Henok 2:1\u20133 &quot;and the Offspring of Seth, who were upon the Holy Mount, saw them and loved them. And they told one another, 'Come, let us choose for us daughters from Cain's children; let us bear children for us.'&quot;<br /> Some individuals and groups, including St. Augustine, John Chrysostom, and John Calvin, take the view of Genesis 6:2 that the &quot;Angels&quot; who fathered the Nephilim referred to certain human males from the lineage of Seth, who were called sons of God probably in reference to their prior covenant with Yahweh (cf. Deuteronomy 14:1; 32:5); according to these sources, these men had begun to pursue bodily interests, and so took wives of &quot;the daughters of men&quot;, e.g., those who were descended from Cain or from any people who did not worship God.<br /> <br /> And we not wandered in to other mythological territories!<br /> The world is filled with stories of Giants<br /> Even up to the modern days<br /> So, I'm curious, have you ever used the said artefact (immagine the Blood Mage who examines the blood and... okay it is from a giant - Divide by cucumber error. Please reinstall universe and reboot.\u200b) and descriptions in the WoD books to smuggle some myths and mysteries in to your games? Any of your palyers decided, lets go to hunt/find these creatur, who may or may not be our progenitor's second (or first...) linage?<br /> Just a little curiosity <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 06-02-2023, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T01:00:55-07:00","id":1513617,"title":"","content":"I would use Formori or Fae for giants. There's a changing breed gift that makes one a giant too. <br /> <br /> But a lot of giants in different mythologies aren't actually big. Greek and Norse &quot;giants&quot; were often normal sized, the big ones were exceptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T10:45:25-07:00","id":1513669,"title":"","content":"Broadly speaking, I think it's a neat idea with fun potential to explore. My familiarity tends to be with later material, so I didn't know Giant's Blood was a thing!<br /> <br /> However, mostly I'm here to clarify that the epithet &quot;Slumbering Giant&quot; is figurative language rather than literal. Before siring Mictlantecuhtli, the Slumbering Giant walked among their people a bit, without any comment besides the usual stuff with vampires (only appears at night, enchanting, a bit stand-offish, etc.). I mean, it is also possible that they *could* be a Giant but used Disciplines to transform or hide their true nature, but it doesn't seem like the intent of the text. They are a &quot;Giant&quot; in the sense of being a plot-device-in-a-can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T12:33:52-07:00","id":1513681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, I'm curious, have you ever used the said artefact (immagine the Blood Mage who examines the blood and... okay it is from a giant - Divide by cucumber error. Please reinstall universe and reboot.\u200b) and descriptions in the WoD books to smuggle some myths and mysteries in to your games? Any of your palyers decided, lets go to hunt/find these creatur, who may or may not be our progenitor's second (or first...) linage?<br /> Just a little curiosity <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> \u200b\u200b </div> </div> </div>I've used sometimes &quot;Blood of Giants&quot; and some players did drink from the bottles, but they never actually met giants. In one of my current stories there's a place (btw a real and amazing place in real life) called <i><b>Eisriesenwelt</b></i>, that in English could be translated as &quot;World of Ice Giants&quot;, one of the main antagonists of the story lives there, and the cave is a powerful Cray, but I still haven't introduced giants per se, but I've tried to. In fact, sometime ago I was thinking about creating Giants (in the sense of giving them traits, as in a character sheet, etc), but haven't found any in the WoD. If I'm not mistaken, not even in the <b>Bygone Bestiary</b>, what is a pity. Perhaps it would make sense to give them high levels of Potence, among other things just to simplify things or make them Fae, but then it's a bit hard to emulate the levels of strength a Giant should have with any other splat powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T13:40:34-07:00","id":1513702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513609-giants?p=1513617#post1513617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would use Formori or Fae for giants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those would be my go to choices if I had to define what was exactly the &quot;giant&quot; who provided the blood for &quot;Giant's Blood&quot; in a WoD setting context. But I also think that is fairly immaterial - the only thing that matters is that this is a remnant of the days when magical creatures like giants once walked the world. It's all part of the context that the Sabbat is heavily involved in exploring ancient occult mysteries and looking for whatever advantage they can get against the Camarilla.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513609-giants#post1513609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm curious, have you ever used the said artefact (immagine the Blood Mage who examines the blood and... okay it is from a giant - Divide by cucumber error. Please reinstall universe and reboot.\u200b) and descriptions in the WoD books to smuggle some myths and mysteries in to your games? Any of your palyers decided, lets go to hunt/find these creatur, who may or may not be our progenitor's second (or first...) linage?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never used any of the artifacts found in the Storyteller's Guide to the Sabbat. Primarily because I have never run or played in Sabbat chronicles. I might be willing to do so if I ran a very occult heavy/oriented chronicle. If I did include it, rather than having it be in the possession of a vampire, it would be more like an object being sought by vampires, and the PCs could decide how to approach the plot (help one of the groups get, concentrate on denying it to one of the groups, or trying to get it for themselves).<br /> <br /> I am much more likely to use such artifacts in my Werewolf chronicles for two reasons. First, Werewolf has a more legendary vibe with stronger connections to the mythic past, the fairy lands, and strange creatures than Vampire does. Second, when I have vampire antagonists in Werewolf, I am much more likely to use the Sabbat (and thus Sabbat adjacent concepts like vampire artifacts). I generally have the Camarilla vampires be more successful in hiding because of the Masquerade so unless the PCs actively go looking for them, I'm just going to have them escape notice unless I have a specific plot in mind. The Sabbat on the other hand is typically much more careless, leave a more obvious trail of blood, travel between cities, and have a culture which encourages foolhardy behavior.<br /> <br /> If I do ever include Giant's Blood specifically, I would pull much more from real world folklore and legends describing it than use WoD game terms, as I feel the latter tends to erode mystery and awe, and the former is more effective in stirring emotions and imaginations from the players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 06-02-2023, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T16:06:11-07:00","id":1513824,"title":"","content":"As much as I like the magic items from early vampire stuff, I also dislike them. I tend to agree with the writers tht they come to represent a mandatory investement on the PC's part if you let them and I think they go against a lot of the themes.<br /> <br /> Also if there are many such items, long lasting, usable by anyone, and dispersed widely enough to end up in various young towns on the pacific coast or the midwest, then it becomes strange that people in the world of darkness aren't aware of them. <br /> <br /> With regards to giants blood, I haven't used it, I can imagine such a thing in the private collection of some autarch elder. I might look to Ars Magica for inspiration as to the origin and nature of different Giants that might have existed in the Classical or Dark Ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","name":"Devidramoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27296_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T17:52:06-07:00","id":1513833,"title":"","content":"I believe someone here on this forum (forgot whom) mentioned the idea of Jotunn as a Nosferatu bloodline. That\u2019d work for giants that are reasonably sized, inhumanly strong, ugly, and man-eating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T01:01:47-07:00","id":1513844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513609-giants?p=1513681#post1513681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In fact, sometime ago I was thinking about creating Giants (in the sense of giving them traits, as in a character sheet, etc), but haven't found any in the WoD. If I'm not mistaken, not even in the <b>Bygone Bestiary</b>, what is a pity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just checked Bygone Bestiary. You CAN make a giant, for a certain value of &quot;giant&quot;, by taking the Size advantage. 10 pts will get you up to &quot;elephant, roc, or whale&quot; size. While you're not a truly colossal figure (like the giant depicted in the art at the start of the character creation section), that certainly qualifies as &quot;giant&quot; in comparison to humans. Less &quot;Attack on Titan&quot;, more &quot;Hill Giant from D&amp;D&quot;. Depending really on how the Storyteller interprets &quot;whale&quot; (or, for that matter, &quot;Roc&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T19:03:08-07:00","id":1514381,"title":"","content":"I agree with Giant's Blood increasing Potence, but also, fortitude as Giant-Size grants an additional health-levels. <br /> <br /> This also reminds me of a book I have called, <i>Before the Pharaohs</i>; it's and archaeology work of pre-dynastic Egypt and they, in the book, found the skulls of giants. It's an interesting read, but, I think I should wear a tin-foil hat while reading it, just to be on the safe-side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T21:09:43-07:00","id":1514392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513609-giants?p=1514381#post1514381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with Giant's Blood increasing Potence, but also, fortitude as Giant-Size grants an additional health-levels.<br /> <br /> This also reminds me of a book I have called, <i>Before the Pharaohs</i>; it's and archaeology work of pre-dynastic Egypt and they, in the book, found the skulls of giants. It's an interesting read, but, I think I should wear a tin-foil hat while reading it, just to be on the safe-side.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the sound of it, a tinfoil is a minimum. Personally I would take an even more drastic approach and just throw that book in the garbage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T23:14:15-07:00","id":1514397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513609-giants?p=1513844#post1513844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just checked Bygone Bestiary. You CAN make a giant, for a certain value of &quot;giant&quot;, by taking the Size advantage. 10 pts will get you up to &quot;elephant, roc, or whale&quot; size. While you're not a truly colossal figure (like the giant depicted in the art at the start of the character creation section), that certainly qualifies as &quot;giant&quot; in comparison to humans. Less &quot;Attack on Titan&quot;, more &quot;Hill Giant from D&amp;D&quot;. Depending really on how the Storyteller interprets &quot;whale&quot; (or, for that matter, &quot;Roc&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something I didn't remember about the book, I need to reread it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T11:45:55-07:00","id":1514490,"title":"","content":"Never heard of &quot;Bygone Bestiary&quot; before to be honest. Maybe something for me to get my hands on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T13:26:19-07:00","id":1514501,"title":"","content":"Whilst I do like Fey Giants, I\u2019m more inclined to have the Giants Blood drawn from lost Crytid giants hidden in lost places.<br /> <br /> Reality deviants that haven\u2019t been driven to extinction or wiped away by the concensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T16:27:48-07:00","id":1515581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513609-giants?p=1514392#post1514392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From the sound of it, a tinfoil is a minimum. Personally I would take an even more drastic approach and just throw that book in the garbage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did pay $10 bucks for it, at a Book-fair; and yeah, <i>Bygone Bestiary</i> is a unique game unto itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":2521,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","user":"Iguazu","date":". 06-19-2023, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count"